<title>USA: Airbus reviews Delta pact as antitrust - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Airbus reviews Delta pact as antitrust - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airbus Industrie is studying the antitrust and trade implications of an exclusive aircraft supply pact which Delta Air Lines announced with rival plane-maker Boeing Co, the Wall Street Journal said in its electronic edition on Friday.</p>
<p>People familiar with the situation said Airbus officials were reviewing the deal, according to the paper.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't think (the Delta deal is) in the best interest of the airline, the shareholders, the employees or the travelling public,&quot; John Leahy, sales chief for the European consortium, was quoted as saying in the paper.</p>
<p>New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
